{"Backup code validation and invalidation flow has a race condition vulnerability where two concurrent login attempts using the same backup code could both succeed before the update persists": 0.8484658598899841, "Backup code validation uses indexOf which performs simple string equality checks, making it vulnerable to timing attacks where attackers could infer information about valid codes based on comparison time": 0.3866494596004486, "JSON.parse of decrypted backup codes lacks error handling - corrupted, malformed, or legacy schema data will throw an unhandled exception": 0.9251407384872437, "Backup codes generated using crypto.randomBytes(5) have smaller code space than TOTP's 6-digit codes, and rate limiting should be applied to backup code login attempts to prevent brute force attacks": 0.5591797828674316, "Missing E2E test coverage for backup code authentication including successful login with backup code, rejection when reusing same code, disabling 2FA with backup code, and error handling for invalid codes": 0.6979153752326965, "JSON.parse in disable.ts lacks error handling for corrupted or malformed encrypted backup code data, which could cause unexpected server errors": 0.9017390608787537}